A||||2||curtis||EGR valve||||1||
Z||000000||curtis||10-26-2000||10:56 PM||||When replacing my brothers egr valve I noticed that there was oil inside the valve itself. Why is this I thought it was only connected to the air intake and the exhaust.||||reg||1
Z||000001||robertjay||10-27-2000||08:05 AM||||The oil may have dripped down from your crank case ventilation that plugs into the intake boot from the airbox (if you have a V-6).  I pulled my boot off when I bought my car and the intake was very black and oily from this hose.  I have since cleaned it and pulled it off now and then and noticed it doesn't get so oily anymore.  Maybe the guy that owned it before me didn't change his oil often enough or something like that.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||10-27-2000||08:40 AM||||Check your PCV valve, It might be going bad and allowing oil into the manifold.  <P>It's located at the end of the tube that runs between the valve cover and to the TBI on a 4 cyl.  For V6 I think it's in the tube robertjay pointed out.  To check if it's bad shake it and you should hear the valve inside rattle, if it doesn't rattle easy it's plugged up.  They're only a couple bucks and it's an easy thing to see if it clears up the problem.  Hope this helps...<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue.gif"> ||||reg||1
